{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791588262,"nonce":"hx6QZ1JCEe4gdx0BL+gRvkguLGs=","message":"The theme system landed in 674c8b5 and c3104fc.\n\n**Paint (674c8b5)**: the host draws `corner-shape` (round, squircle, bevel, scoop, notch, square or superellipse(n), one to four values, and `locked`), `box-shadow` (outer layers; inset is reported as unsupported) and letter spacing in em. The node's corner shape and locked flag reach the native paint props (PaintStyle.cornerShape and cornerShapeLocked in the addon), so blinc_abi's Shapes::resolve sees explicit and locked shapes.\n\n**Theme (c3104fc)**: `blinc_ts/theme`.\n- Typed token sets: colours (38 semantic names), typography (families, sizes, weights, leading, tracking in em), spacing steps, radii, shadow stacks, durations and easings (named, cubic-bezier, steps; `ease()` evaluates them), and ShapeTokens.\n- Theme (one scheme) and ThemeBundle (light, dark, optional stylesheets); `extendTheme` and `extendBundle` make variants; `defineTheme` and the scale helpers build one. `neutralTheme` is a grey bundle for tests and examples, not Blinc's.\n- `themeVariables(theme)` gives every token as a custom property with Blinc's names (`--surface-elevated`, `--space-4`, `--radius-lg`, `--shadow-md`, `--ease-spring`, ...), plus `--corner-smoothing`, `--corner-exponent`, `--smoothing-threshold` and `--corner-n`.\n- ThemeState holds the bundle, the scheme preference (light, dark, system), the system scheme and overrides in signals of a ReactiveContext; `theme` and `variables` are computeds. `attach(layout)` is an effect that calls setTheme, setColorScheme and the new `Layout.setShape`, and swaps the bundle's sheets when the bundle changes. `followSystem(windowHost)` reads Window.theme() and ThemeChanged events (no polling).\n- Shape: effective exponent = 2 + (max(e, 2) - 2) x clamp(s, 0, 1), n = log2 as an f32 fraction; off when smoothing \u003c= 0.001 or the threshold is infinite (n = 0). `Layout.setShape(tokens, radiusFull)` makes it the default of prepareDisplayList; paint options that set cornerShape still win. A sheet's `:root { corner-smoothing; corner-exponent; smoothing-threshold }` stands over the theme's, read from the root's restyle.\n- `blinc_ts/theme/utilities` (optional): `utilityCss()`, `addUtilities(layout)`, `utilityClasses` and a `UtilityClass` type with `classes(...)`; bg-/text-/border- colours, spacing prefixes (p-0.5 escaped), rounded, shadow, text sizes, font weights and families, leading, tracking, corner shapes.\n\n**Tests**: tests/theme.test.mjs (formula, hybrid 0.4/3.3/12 gives n = 1.3334237337112427, off semantics, lerp, colours, easings, variables, variants, utilities). tests/native-theme.mjs renders offscreen: a light-to-dark switch changes pixels and keeps geometry; overrides, spacing relayout, system scheme from window events, bundle sheets swapped; with the hybrid shape the fill, border, shadow and inherited-clip corners change while a radius under the threshold, a pill and a `round locked` box stay pixel-identical, an explicit squircle is unchanged, `:root { corner-smoothing: 0 }` restores the round frame exactly, and invalid corner-shape values are reported.\n\n**Not done here**: animated scheme transitions (colours switch at once); transition/duration utilities and variants (hover:, dark:), since the host has no CSS transitions yet; inset shadows; glass is covered only by blinc_abi's shared shape resolution, not by a pixel test.","files":null}]}